2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"The executor fully satisfied the task contract: it established a healthy 3-member etcd cluster with application keys, directly demonstrated node3's permanent loss with quorum preserved on node1/node2, removed the dead member and added a working replacement member on node3, and directly confirmed the cluster returned to 3/3 healthy members with all original keys intact and replicated to the new node3 member. The independent, mandatory node-restart evidence protocol was also completed to a high standard on all three nodes, with pre-restart boot identity, restart acknowledgement, changed post-restart boot identity (cross-checked exactly against the fixed lifecycle snapshots), and recovered cluster/data state each directly observed. Hygiene is good overall; the only blemish is unreverted temporary install artifacts left in /tmp on each node and one benign systemd readiness timeout during initial bootstrap that self-resolved.","limitations":["No evidence was captured of etcd's internal raft/member-sync logs during the node3 rejoin beyond endpoint status and key reads, so the exact resynchronization mechanism (snapshot vs. log replay) is inferred rather than directly observed, though the outcome (data present, correct raft indices) is directly confirmed.","The before_prepare and after_prepare snapshots are identical aliases (prepare disabled), so no preparer-introduced state could be distinguished from executor changes; all after_executor deltas are attributable to the executor by elimination."]},"ttft_ms":31757,"type":"result","duration_ms":78525,"uuid":"8410f3c1-af88-4ccf-bcc6-b7dcf2f8b2eb","ttft_stream_ms":956,"time_to_request_ms":40,"first_content_frame_ms":1504,"queued_turn_count":0}
